The allocation preference is \emph{non-monotonic}. We observe three qualitative behaviors at the sampled sparsity levels (7--8B scale):

\noindent\textbf{Budget-surplus ($\leq$30\%).}
Uniform allocation provides $7.5\times$ smaller cross-seed MMLU standard deviation ($\sigma$: 1.3pp vs.\ 9.5pp), eliminating catastrophic seed-dependent degradation under global top-$k$ (MMLU 35.7$\pm$9.5\% vs.\ 40.7$\pm$1.3\%, 3-seed). Global top-$k$ starves late layers (L31: 28.4\%, std/mean$=$1.89), and this starvation interacts unpredictably with predictor initialization (Appendix~\ref{app:lagrangian}). % exp_id: kl30_3seed

\noindent\textbf{Budget-constrained ($\sim$40\%).}
The preference reverses: global achieves MMLU 38.06\% vs.\ uniform's 30.68\% (+7.4pp). % exp_id: bench_kl40_global, d030_kl40_uniform
PPL remains low (8.36) but downstream accuracy degrades, confirming PPL is a poor proxy for reasoning.

\noindent\textbf{Capacity-limited ($\geq$50\%).}
Global/uniform gap vanishes (MMLU 27.89\% vs.\ 27.77\%, both $\approx$ random). % exp_id: bench_kl50_global, d030_kl50_uniform
Late-layer starvation persists across levels (L24--31 retention: 50.1/34.2/22.6\% at 30/50/70\% sparsity; Figure~\ref{fig:retention}), consistent on both 7--8B models (\S\ref{sec:cross_arch}).

\paragraph{Gap Decomposition.}
Decomposing the Dense$\to$KL gap under uniform allocation (5.85 PPL): per-token hard mask evaluation (Appendix~\ref{app:db_sensitivity}) yields PPL 9.22, attributing 53\% to predictor approximation (including discretization) and 47\% to per-layer budget allocation.
Even under global allocation, the learned predictor (11.79) remains $1.98\times$ better than TEAL (23.31), confirming distributional training captures neuron interactions that magnitude scoring misses.


\subsection{SPON Orthogonality Analysis}
\label{sec:spon}

At 50\% sparsity, the predictor's hidden-state perturbation (L2=482.65) and SPON's additive correction (L2=76.2, cosine similarity 0.196) are weakly correlated ($R^2$=0.038); SPON yields only 2.4\% PPL improvement (12.08$\to$11.79), confirming the KL predictor already captures most recoverable signal. % exp_id: spon_decomposition, spon_2048_s42, mvp_kl_norm_v2_s42

